From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Faruk Nehir <omerfaruknehir@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 07:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: force X1E80100 CSID teardown/reconfigure
 on stream switches

On X1E80100, rapidly tearing down one camera stream and starting another
can leave the Gen3 CSID in stale state. The following stream then reaches
VIDIOC_STREAMON but times out waiting for frames.

The generic csid_set_stream() path currently calls configure_stream() only
when phy.need_vc_update is set. After a successful start that flag is
cleared, so a stop that does not coincide with a link or power-state update
can skip the Gen3 disable writes entirely.

For X1E80100 only, always apply the CSID disable sequence on s_stream(0) and
mark the VC configuration dirty so the next s_stream(1) necessarily
reprograms the path.

This is intentionally scoped to X1E80100 while the rapid RGB/IR switching
failure is being validated on the ASUS Zenbook A14.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
@@ -758,6 +758,18 @@ static int csid_set_stream(struct v4l2_subdev *sd, int enable)
 	struct csid_device *csid = v4l2_get_subdevdata(sd);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * X1E80100 Gen3 CSID can retain an enabled RDI configuration when
+	 * userspace switches cameras quickly enough that the CSID does not go
+	 * through a full power/link reconfiguration between streams.  Make
+	 * stream-off explicit and force the next stream-on to reprogram the VC.
+	 */
+	if (!enable && csid->camss->res->version == CAMSS_X1E80100) {
+		csid->res->hw_ops->configure_stream(csid, false);
+		csid->phy.need_vc_update = true;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (enable) {
 		if (csid->testgen.nmodes != CSID_PAYLOAD_MODE_DISABLED) {
 			ret = v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup(&csid->ctrls);
-- 
2.43.0
